A hint file that fails to read during DB::open kills the process instead of
being rebuilt from its data file: the behaviour recovery had while it
memory-mapped hint files, where the kernel's SIGBUS did it. #255 (#237)
replaced the mapping with pread; this restores the symptom (by abort()), not
the mapping.
Expected: caught.
